          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "门 — mén — \"door; gate\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "这是我家的门 zhè shì wǒ jiā de mén — This is the door to my home."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 门 (mén) — a dot, a post down the left, and a frame that turns down the right and hooks: the right-hand piece of 们. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "门 (mén) is inherited from Middle Chinese mwon (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription); the dictionary says its old character is made of two door leaves."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
